From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yevhen Salitrynskyi <ysalitrynskyi@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 20:07:44 -0500
Subject: feat: import from Opera

Opera joins the Chromium family's sources: a block of its own on welcome step 2,
which Settings' and the command bar's import rows open. Bookmarks, history and
passwords come in as they do from Chrome, into "Imported from Opera".

It differs in three ways. Its data is under its own name, com.operasoftware.Opera
on the Mac and Opera Software\Opera Stable under %APPDATA% on Windows, not
%LOCALAPPDATA%. A version from before it had profiles keeps the profile's files in
that folder itself, with no list of profiles, so with nothing else there the
folder is the profile. And most of a person's bookmarks are in roots of its own
under custom_root: its folders and the unsorted ones come in; Speed Dial, the
trash and the pinboards do not.

A browser test now finds a browser of the family, or Arc, only in a folder it
made. Any test that opened the welcome flow looked in the machine's own folders,
and counted what a browser it found held there.

Why: import I43 (BACKLOG S-375). Opera could not be imported at all, and the file
shapes were confirmed in public migrators and importers first.
Removable when: the family's import leaves the series.
